WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
After Zann left, Fala went back upstairs.

2
00:00:03.661 --> 00:00:11.884
Teplo busied himself reading some papers. Perda finished the food Fala had conjured and looked around, feeling restless and worried about Zann.

3
00:00:11.885 --> 00:00:17.886
"I wish we could do something useful," she told Darb. "I hate just sitting here."

4
00:00:17.887 --> 00:00:22.978
Darb didn't answer. He was staring into space. Perda poked him in the arm.

5
00:00:22.979 --> 00:00:28.898
"Huh?" he said. "Oh, sorry. I was just thinking about Zing. I hope he's okay."

6
00:00:28.899 --> 00:00:34.219
"I'm sure he's fine," Perda said. "I wish we could get him back though."

7
00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:38.025
Teplo looked over. "Who are you talking about?"

8
00:00:38.026 --> 00:00:46.214
"Zann's pet dragon," Perda said. "Remember? We told you the palace people took him away when he tried to burn down the door."

9
00:00:46.215 --> 00:00:49.407
Teplo's face lit up. "I think I can help."

10
00:00:49.408 --> 00:00:55.652
He let out a sharp whistle. A moment later they heard a rustle of feathers from a dark corner of the room.

11
00:00:55.653 --> 00:00:59.549
Then a large waterfowl waddled into view.

12
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.713
"What's that?" Darb took a step toward the creature.

13
00:01:02.714 --> 00:01:06.041
"Careful," Teplo said as the bird snapped at Darb.

14
00:01:06.042 --> 00:01:09.616
"She's rather foul-tempered. She's a sniffer goose."

15
00:01:09.617 --> 00:01:15.702
"A what?" Darb looked confused. "I've never heard of that species. Where do they come from?"

16
00:01:15.703 --> 00:01:21.496
"A sniffer goose is a creature whose entire purpose is tracking dragons," Teplo said.

17
00:01:21.497 --> 00:01:25.759
"If you describe Zann's dragon, she should be able to retrieve him."

18
00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:31.248
Perda noticed that the old man hadn't answered Darb's question about where the sniffer goose was from.

19
00:01:31.249 --> 00:01:35.932
But she didn't really care. If they could get Zing back, Zann would be thrilled.

20
00:01:35.933 --> 00:01:42.452
"Zing's a fire whistler," she said. "He's kind of small, with reddish-bronze scales."

21
00:01:42.453 --> 00:01:46.293
She and Darb went on to describe Zing as well as they could.

22
00:01:46.294 --> 00:01:51.835
Teplo listened and translated their description into a series of whistles, grunts, and clicks.

23
00:01:51.836 --> 00:01:54.308
The goose tilted her head and listened.

24
00:01:54.309 --> 00:01:58.333
"You speak this bird's language?" Darb asked, looking impressed.

25
00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:02.477
"I speak sniffer goose well enough to get by." Teplo shrugged.

26
00:02:02.478 --> 00:02:09.868
"It's an easy language to learn. It's even simpler than Troll, and just about anyone can learn that with little trouble."

27
00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:14.989
"If you say so." Perda watched the bird. "Now what happens?"

28
00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:20.297
"Go, my feathered friend!" Teplo fluttered his hands at the goose and let out a honk.

29
00:02:20.298 --> 00:02:24.085
The sniffer goose honked loudly in reply and flapped her wings.

30
00:02:24.086 --> 00:02:27.094
Teplo pulled on a lever, opening the trapdoor.

31
00:02:27.095 --> 00:02:31.524
Honking eagerly, the goose flew up and out.

32
00:02:31.525 --> 00:02:37.298
Teplo closed the trapdoor and smiled at the kids. "Now we wait."

33
00:02:37.299 --> 00:02:44.013
"Who are you?" Zann asked as he floated along behind the mysterious people. "Where are you taking me?"

34
00:02:44.014 --> 00:02:48.430
"Hurry." One of the people shoved Zann's bubble through a doorway.

35
00:02:48.431 --> 00:02:56.057
The bubble touched down and faded, and Zann found himself in a windowless room, face to face with Yog.

36
00:02:56.058 --> 00:02:59.798
Zann gasped. "Did you come to take me back to the palace?" Yog

37
00:02:59.799 --> 00:03:06.655
grinned at him. "Not exactly. But you should have seen Rixa's face when she found out that you four were gone!" Zann

38
00:03:06.656 --> 00:03:14.550
was confused. He glanced at the others, but he didn't recognize any of them. "Then why—" "Zann!"

39
00:03:14.551 --> 00:03:19.606
a woman's voice interrupted. "It's a pleasure to meet you." Zann

40
00:03:19.607 --> 00:03:24.233
turned around. A tall, imposing woman had just entered. "This

41
00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:29.742
is Venna," Yog said. "She's one of the few remaining free members of the Red Council." Zann

42
00:03:29.743 --> 00:03:34.906
had heard of Venna, one of the strongest Magic Masters of her generation. "Nice

43
00:03:34.907 --> 00:03:37.712
to meet you too," he said. "Sorry

44
00:03:37.713 --> 00:03:42.282
we had to grab you off the street like that, Zann," Venna said. "But

45
00:03:42.283 --> 00:03:44.778
it's not safe for you out there. When

46
00:03:44.779 --> 00:03:49.316
I got Teplo's message, I immediately sent my associates to fetch you. On

47
00:03:49.317 --> 00:03:53.916
their way they spotted you and decided to intercept you before the trolls did." "I

48
00:03:53.917 --> 00:03:56.890
was fine," Zann protested. "Indeed,"

49
00:03:56.891 --> 00:04:02.790
Venna said. "I'm thrilled that you've eluded the trolls this long. You

50
00:04:02.791 --> 00:04:06.661
must be just as talented as Boz and your parents." "My

51
00:04:06.662 --> 00:04:11.590
parents?" Zann said. "Do—did you know them?" "Of

52
00:04:11.591 --> 00:04:19.524
course! Everyone in First City knew of their fascinating research and mourned the loss of their genius." Zann

53
00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.033
wasn't sure what to say to that. Luckily

54
00:04:22.034 --> 00:04:25.541
Venna didn't seem to expect him to say anything. "That's

55
00:04:25.542 --> 00:04:29.910
why I'm so confident you're the right choice," she said. "The

56
00:04:29.911 --> 00:04:33.278
right choice for what?" Zann asked. Venna

57
00:04:33.279 --> 00:04:44.840
smiled. "To become the next king of Magica." "What

58
00:04:44.841 --> 00:04:51.105
do you want?" Morb snapped at the troll who had just entered. "Can't you see that I'm busy?" The

59
00:04:51.106 --> 00:04:53.216
troll didn't respond for a moment. It

60
00:04:53.217 --> 00:04:57.455
stared at Morb's new contraption, fear in its dull eyes. "Well?"

61
00:04:57.456 --> 00:05:00.446
Morb said impatiently. The

62
00:05:00.447 --> 00:05:03.550
troll finally looked at him and let out a grunt. An

63
00:05:03.551 --> 00:05:07.281
image formed briefly above its head and then sputtered out. Morb

64
00:05:07.282 --> 00:05:15.468
frowned. "Was that the boy—Boz's grandson?" he demanded. "Did you idiots finally capture him?" The

65
00:05:15.469 --> 00:05:22.076
troll shook its head. Another puff of magical energy showed Zann with a crown on his head. "What?"

66
00:05:22.077 --> 00:05:27.712
Morb exclaimed. "They're making him king ? Impossible!"

67
00:05:27.713 --> 00:05:31.784
The troll grunted, but Morb had never bothered to learn its language.

68
00:05:31.785 --> 00:05:38.535
Morb was tempted to stop what he was doing to find out more but he decided against it. Soon it wouldn't matter.

69
00:05:38.536 --> 00:05:41.425
Morb looked at his contraption with satisfaction.

70
00:05:41.426 --> 00:05:46.532
The pythons the old woman had brought were writhing in a large glass tube in the middle.

71
00:05:46.533 --> 00:05:50.987
The bone-and-wire frame filled most of the space in the underground room.

72
00:05:50.988 --> 00:05:58.759
Soon, very soon now, it would be time to move it to a larger location, and Morb had a particular spot in mind.

73
00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:01.654
There Morb would have more space to work.

74
00:06:01.655 --> 00:06:08.985
There he would be able to find the few remaining parts he needed.

